<p><br />Earn your degree in Hospitality Business Management with Washington State University Everett right here in beautiful South Lake Tahoe.</p>
<p>Course offerings through Washington State University Everett will help you master the fundamentals of operating hotels, restaurants, managed services venues, and tourism destinations&mdash;whether they&rsquo;re located in the U.S. or around the world.</p>
<p><a href="https://online.wsu.edu/undergrad/HBM.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="" src="https://www.ltcc.edu/_resources/images/wsu_everett.png" alt="WSU Everett logo" width="360" height="80" /></a></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 24px;"><br />Coming Up in Spring 2025:<br /></span>May 12, 2025 - June 22, 2025</p>
<div>
<p class="p1"><strong>HBM280 Hospitality Systems</strong><br /><em>HBM280 </em>|&nbsp;<em>Monday + Wednesday from 9am - 12pm</em><strong><br /></strong>3 Management functions relating to the planning and operation of various lodging, food, and beverage businesses.</p>
</div>
<div><strong>HBM358 Food Service Systems and Control</strong></div>
<div><em>HBM358 </em>|&nbsp;<em>Tuesday + Thursday from 9am-12pm</em></div>
<div>3 Course Prerequisite: ACCTG 230 or 298; B A 204, 205, and <span style="font-size: inherit; background-color: #fffdfd;">206 or concurrent enrollment, or B A 212 or concurrent enrollment; admitted to a major in the College</span>
<p class="p1">of Business or minor in Hospitality Business Management. Operational control processes, control systems, and cost analysis procedures in food and beverage management.</p>
<p class="p1"><strong>HBM 496 Special Topics<br /></strong>V 1-3 May be repeated for credit: cumulative maximum 6 credits.<br /><span style="font-size: inherit; background-color: #fffdfd;">HBM 496</span><span style="font-size: inherit; background-color: #fffdfd;"> will be structured as an industry sponsored project provided by local industry partners. </span><em style="font-size: inherit;">This will be a full 12-week course | May 5<span class="s1">th -</span>&nbsp;July 25<span class="s1">th</span>.<br /></em><span style="font-size: inherit; background-color: #fffdfd;">This project would be outside of any industry experience hours. We will require HBM 496 plus a minimum of one of the two courses. Industry mentors and Instructor will collaborate on progress meetings and expectations.</span></p>
</div>
<div>For more information about how to register for classes, call 530.541.4660 x245 or email <a href="mailto:lmuc@ltcc.edu">lmuc@ltcc.edu</a>.</div>
<hr />
<h5>About the LTCC/WSU Everett Partnership</h5>
<p>In 2018, Lake Tahoe Community College entered into an agreement with Washington State University, a top-tiered research institution, to offer a degree in Hospitality Business Management (HBM). Courses are offered on campus at the Lisa Maloff University Center through WSU Everett.</p>
<hr />
<h5>About WSU&rsquo;s School of Hospitality Business Management</h5>
<p>WSU&rsquo;s <a href="https://business.wsu.edu/departments/hospitality/">School of Hospitality Business Management,</a> established in 1932, consistently ranks among the top 5 percent of the 170 similar programs in the nation. It is part of WSU&rsquo;s AACSB-accredited <a href="https://business.wsu.edu/">Carson College of Business</a>. Our alumni live and work across the globe.</p>
<hr />
<h5>Financial Support</h5>
<p>Financial support is available through LTCC and WSU.</p>
<p><strong>Scholarship Opportunities</strong></p>
<p>For more information about LTCC scholarships, email <a href="mailto:mailto:%20ucenter@ltcc.edu">ucenter@ltcc.edu</a>.</p>
<div>
<p><span style="background-color: #fffdfd;">WSU&rsquo;s School of Hospitality Business Management awards over $125,000 in scholarships annually. The Carson College of Business awarded its students over $800,000 during the 2019-2020 academic year; scholarships range from $500 to $5,000 per recipient per year, and students are eligible to receive more than one scholarship. </span><a href="https://business.wsu.edu/next-carson-coug/scholarships/getting-started/">Learn more and apply for scholarships here</a><span style="background-color: #fffdfd;">.</span></p>
<p><strong>Financial Aid</strong></p>
</div>
<p>Students in the HBM program are also eligible to apply for financial aid. Additional assistance is available! Contact Brandon Buckingham at <a href="mailto:brandon.buckingham@wsu.edu">brandon.buckingham@wsu.edu</a>.</p>
<p><strong>For Tahoe-based students who are interested in applying or who may need financial assistance, please contact Meredith Crosby, <a href="mailto:mecrosby@ltcc.edu">mecrosby@ltcc.edu</a> with the ADVANCE Office at LTCC.</strong></p>
<hr />
